import{_ as l,C as p,o as s,c as m,a2 as d,b as i,w as a,a as o,E as n,a3 as c,j as r}from"./chunks/framework.BDCokyix.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"End-to-End Flows (Soma)","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"architecture/e2e-flows.md","filePath":"architecture/e2e-flows.md","lastUpdated":1780254295000}'),h={name:"architecture/e2e-flows.md"};function u(b,e,f,A,k,T){const t=p("Mermaid");return s(),m("div",null,[e[4]||(e[4]=d('<h1 id="end-to-end-flows-soma" tabindex="-1">End-to-End Flows (Soma) <a class="header-anchor" href="#end-to-end-flows-soma" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;End-to-End Flows (Soma)&quot;">​</a></h1><p>This page documents a few &quot;follow the bytes&quot; flows across the repo so you can orient yourself when changing UI, daemon, or peer code.</p><h2 id="_1-desktop-renderer-↔-tauri-host-with-in-process-daemon" tabindex="-1">1) Desktop renderer ↔ Tauri host (with in-process daemon) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-desktop-renderer-↔-tauri-host-with-in-process-daemon" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1) Desktop renderer ↔ Tauri host (with in-process daemon)&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>The desktop app lives under <code>desktop/desktop-app</code> (a Tauri V2 shell). The React/Vite renderer is in <code>src/</code>; the Rust host is in <code>src-tauri/</code>. Tapia&#39;s <code>/practice</code> route is planned but not yet wired into the renderer router.</li><li>The peer / daemon runtime is <code>soma-daemon</code> (<code>backend/crates/daemon</code>, library only), embedded by the host&#39;s <code>desktop-daemon</code> crate and run in-process. There is no separate daemon process and no IPC socket.</li><li>The renderer reaches the host through <code>@soma/sdk</code> over Tauri commands (<code>createBackend(tauriTransport())</code>); wire types are generated from the Rust command graph via <code>tauri-specta</code>. The <code>proto/daemon/v1/daemon.proto</code> schema is Rust-only (libp2p wire formats), not a renderer transport.</li></ul><p>High-level sequence:</p>',5)),(s(),i(c,null,{default:a(()=>[n(t,{id:"mermaid-29",class:"mermaid",graph:"sequenceDiagram%0A%20%20participant%20R%20as%20Renderer%20(React%20%2B%20%40soma%2Fsdk)%0A%20%20participant%20M%20as%20Tauri%20host%20(src-tauri)%20%2B%20soma-daemon%20(in-process)%0A%0A%20%20R-%3E%3EM%3A%20command%3A%20status()%0A%20%20M--%3E%3ER%3A%20peerId%20%2B%20listenAddrs%0A%20%20R-%3E%3EM%3A%20subscribe%20to%20daemon%20events%0A%20%20M--%3E%3ER%3A%20Tauri%20event%20stream%20of%20DaemonEvent%0A"})]),fallback:a(()=>[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o(" Loading... ",-1)])]),_:1})),e[5]||(e[5]=d('<h2 id="_2-join-a-space-membership-capabilities" tabindex="-1">2) Join a space (membership capabilities) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-join-a-space-membership-capabilities" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2) Join a space (membership capabilities)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Flow summary:</p><ol><li>The renderer asks the Tauri host (via <code>@soma/sdk</code>) to join a space.</li><li>The in-process daemon sends a join request over libp2p.</li><li>A bot (or owner/issuer peer) decides and returns a join decision.</li><li>The daemon persists the outcome and the renderer is notified through the event stream.</li></ol><p>Relevant code:</p><ul><li>Command handler: <code>desktop/desktop-api</code> (transport-agnostic) surfaced as a <code>#[tauri::command]</code> in <code>desktop/desktop-commands</code>; the renderer calls it through <code>@soma/sdk</code>.</li><li>Peer protocol wiring: <code>backend/crates/peer/src/lib.rs</code> (protocol id <code>/soma/join/1</code>).</li><li>Bot join decider wiring: <code>backend/bins/somad/src/commands/bot/runtime.rs</code>.</li><li>Daemon join handling: <code>backend/crates/daemon/src/handle/joins.rs</code>, <code>backend/crates/daemon/src/handlers/</code>.</li></ul>',5)),(s(),i(c,null,{default:a(()=>[n(t,{id:"mermaid-83",class:"mermaid",graph:"sequenceDiagram%0A%20%20participant%20R%20as%20Renderer%20(%40soma%2Fsdk)%0A%20%20participant%20M%20as%20Tauri%20host%20%2B%20soma-daemon%20(in-process)%0A%20%20participant%20Bot%20as%20somad%20bot%20(remote%20peer)%0A%0A%20%20R-%3E%3EM%3A%20command%3A%20joinSpace(space_id%2C%20target_peer_id%2C%20addrs)%0A%20%20M-%3E%3EBot%3A%20%2Fsoma%2Fjoin%2F1%20JoinRequest%20(libp2p)%0A%20%20Bot--%3E%3EM%3A%20%2Fsoma%2Fjoin%2F1%20JoinDecision%0A%20%20M--%3E%3ER%3A%20event%3A%20joinSubmitted%20%2F%20joinDecision%0A"})]),fallback:a(()=>[...e[1]||(e[1]=[o(" Loading... ",-1)])]),_:1})),e[6]||(e[6]=d('<p>See also: <code>docs/src/architecture/space-membership.md</code>.</p><h2 id="_3-blob-upload-desktop-and-references" tabindex="-1">3) Blob upload (desktop) and references <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-blob-upload-desktop-and-references" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3) Blob upload (desktop) and references&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Design rule:</p><ul><li>Collaborative documents store <strong>references</strong> to blobs, not bytes.</li><li>The daemon owns blob persistence; bots are cache-only.</li></ul><p>On desktop, the renderer invokes an upload command through <code>@soma/sdk</code> (<code>desktop-commands</code> → <code>desktop-api</code>), which hands the bytes to the in-process daemon to publish into the content-addressed store.</p><p>See: <code>docs/src/architecture/blobs-vdfs.md</code>.</p><h2 id="_4-fetch-a-blob-by-cid-with-cache-peer" tabindex="-1">4) Fetch a blob by CID (with cache peer) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-fetch-a-blob-by-cid-with-cache-peer" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;4) Fetch a blob by CID (with cache peer)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Flow summary:</p><ol><li>A peer requests bytes for <code>(space_id, cid)</code> over <code>/soma/blob/1</code>.</li><li>The remote peer reads from its blob provider (daemon store or bot cache).</li><li>The requester verifies the CID before persisting/serving.</li></ol><p>Current note:</p><ul><li>Blob serving is membership-gated at the peer layer; this is not an open fetch path for non-members.</li></ul><p>Relevant code:</p><ul><li>Protocol id: <code>backend/crates/peer/src/lib.rs</code> (<code>/soma/blob/1</code>).</li><li>Provider boundary: <code>backend/crates/vdfs/src/lib.rs</code> (<code>BlobProvider</code>).</li><li>Filesystem implementation: <code>backend/crates/vdfs/src/fs.rs</code> (<code>soma_vdfs::fs::FsBlobStore</code>, used by both the in-process daemon and the server bot).</li></ul>',13)),(s(),i(c,null,{default:a(()=>[n(t,{id:"mermaid-164",class:"mermaid",graph:"sequenceDiagram%0A%20%20participant%20A%20as%20Requesting%20peer%20(desktop%20in-process)%0A%20%20participant%20B%20as%20Serving%20peer%20(desktop%20or%20somad%20bot)%0A%0A%20%20A-%3E%3EB%3A%20BlobRequest(cid%2C%20space_id)%0A%20%20B--%3E%3EA%3A%20BlobResponse(found%2C%20data)%0A%20%20Note%20over%20A%3A%20verify%20CID%20before%20persisting%0A"})]),fallback:a(()=>[...e[2]||(e[2]=[o(" Loading... ",-1)])]),_:1})),e[7]||(e[7]=d('<h2 id="_5-model-chat-renderer-→-main-→-provider" tabindex="-1">5) Model chat (renderer → main → provider) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-model-chat-renderer-→-main-→-provider" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5) Model chat (renderer → main → provider)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The desktop renderer initiates a chat request through <code>@soma/sdk</code> over Tauri commands. Chat / list-models / rerank go to an OpenAI-compatible HTTP endpoint configured in the Tauri store (Ollama or a remote provider) and driven by the <code>desktop-agent</code> client. The agent library (<code>soma-agentd</code>, embedded in-process) is used only for in-process drift resolution and status; it does <strong>not</strong> proxy model RPCs.</p><p>Relevant code (desktop side):</p><ul><li>Renderer chat surface: <code>desktop/desktop-app/src</code> (consumes <code>@soma/sdk</code>).</li><li>Host agent client: <code>desktop/desktop-agent</code> (OpenAI-compatible chat/embed/rerank).</li></ul>',4)),(s(),i(c,null,{default:a(()=>[n(t,{id:"mermaid-186",class:"mermaid",graph:"sequenceDiagram%0A%20%20participant%20R%20as%20Renderer%20(React%20%2B%20%40soma%2Fsdk)%0A%20%20participant%20M%20as%20Tauri%20host%20(desktop-agent)%0A%20%20participant%20P%20as%20OpenAI-compatible%20endpoint%20(Ollama%20%2F%20remote)%0A%0A%20%20R-%3E%3EM%3A%20chatStream(messages)%0A%20%20M-%3E%3EP%3A%20POST%20%2Fv1%2Fchat%2Fcompletions%20(stream%3Dtrue)%0A%20%20P--%3E%3EM%3A%20SSE%20token%20chunks%0A%20%20M--%3E%3ER%3A%20Tauri%20event%20stream%20of%20token%20events%0A"})]),fallback:a(()=>[...e[3]||(e[3]=[o(" Loading... ",-1)])]),_:1})),e[8]||(e[8]=r("h2",{id:"_6-server-llm-bff-optional",tabindex:"-1"},[o("6) Server LLM BFF (optional) "),r("a",{class:"header-anchor",href:"#_6-server-llm-bff-optional","aria-label":'Permalink to "6) Server LLM BFF (optional)"'},"​")],-1)),e[9]||(e[9]=r("p",null,[r("code",null,"somad bff"),o(" exposes an Axum HTTP API intended for deployments where LLM-backed features run on a server. It can be configured to call an external model HTTP endpoint.")],-1)),e[10]||(e[10]=r("p",null,[o("See: "),r("code",null,"backend/bins/somad/src/commands/bff/"),o(" and "),r("code",null,"backend/crates/bff/"),o(".")],-1))])}const v=l(h,[["render",u]]);export{g as __pageData,v as default};
